// PDF-97 D7. NEW. The production-posture section: the page's answer to "is
// this ready, and where are the bugs" -- a question the site had no
// section for before this item. Its section id is `status`, the last id
// the published anchor set (`sections.ts`/`Navbar.astro`) reserves.
// (Deliberately not spelled as a literal `id=` example in this comment:
// `tests/test_website_contract.py`'s AR2/AR4 scan `website/src` for
// exactly that attribute shape, and a worked example here would double-
// count as one of its own targets -- the same reason `sections.ts` and
// `LicenseSummary.astro` give for the identical omission.)
//
// Three claims, each carrying a verbatim source anchor into `README.md`,
// checked by `tests/test_website_contract.py`'s `SOURCE_ANCHORS` table
// (D8): the output/exit-code contract is public API frozen at v1.0.0
// (P1); open defects live in the maintainer's planning tree and that tree
// is not part of this distribution (P2); Phase 1 (v1) is complete (P3).
//
// Four things this section deliberately never names (D7, AC9): a sweep id,
// a commit sha, an open-finding tally, and a version number outside the
// one sanctioned, frozen phrase "public API from v1.0.0" -- which is a
// historical fact that never rots, not a claim about the current release.
// This section states WHERE defects are recorded and WHAT is frozen, never
// HOW MANY are open right now and never WHICH build. `README.md`'s own
// `## Known issues` section is the live pointer with a real count; this
// page is not a second copy of it and does not try to stay in sync with a
// number that is wrong the day after it is written.
//
// Boundary with `ClosingCta.astro` (D7): the DCO line, the install command
// and the three ranked destinations are that component's, and this one
// does not restate them.
---

<section id="status" class="u-crop mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-24">
  <p class="micro text-surface-400">Production posture</p>
  <div class="u-reveal-rule mt-3 h-px w-full bg-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <h2 class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-surface-50 sm:text-4xl">
    Is this ready, and where the defects are recorded
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-surface-300">
    Three facts about the project, not a live count.
  </p>

  <dl class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
    <div class="card p-4">
      <dt class="micro text-primary-400">Public API</dt>
      <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-snug text-surface-200">
        The structured output shapes and the exit-code table are public API from v1.0.0.
        Breaking either requires a major version bump and a
        <code class="code-inline text-xs">schema_version</code> increment.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div class="card p-4">
      <dt class="micro text-primary-400">Open defects</dt>
      <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-snug text-surface-200">
        Open defects and planned work are recorded, per finding, in the maintainer's planning
        tree -- <code class="code-inline text-xs">BACKLOG.md</code> and
        <code class="code-inline text-xs">qa/FINDINGS-LEDGER.md</code>. Those artifacts are not
        part of this distribution: they are not shipped in the sdist or the wheel and are not
        present in a clone.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div class="card p-4">
      <dt class="micro text-primary-400">Phase</dt>
      <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-snug text-surface-200">
        Phase 1 (v1) complete. Per-spec status and the rest of the planned work live in that
        same tree.
      </dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>
